  clock: 4  # c284
  nonce: c284  # c284
  message: "ADDENDUM (WI-lihis): two more declared levels belong in this row's per-attribute table beside the precedence order — merge_producers.CORROBORATED_CONFIDENCE (0.95, §13) and finalize.SUPERSEDED_STUB_RANK_FACTOR (0.5, §14). Both are module constants today; both should become preferences in the same [merge] section, non-trust (they execute nothing)."  # c284
- op: discuss  # 7c3d
  at: '2026-09-19T08:35:58Z'  # 7c3d
  by: agent  # 7c3d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7c3d
  clock: 5  # 7c3d
  nonce: 7c3d  # 7c3d
  message: "Handoff from WI-dajif (PR #1078). The instrument exists: `hypergumbo backend-agreement`; the first committed table is docs/audits/0019 (kind: backend_agreement), regenerated by scripts/regenerate-backend-agreement-table. ADR-0057 §5 now reads \"a citation names a docs/audits/ document of kind: backend_agreement\" — so the config.toml default this row builds can carry per-attribute exceptions ONLY with such a citation, and a declared exception without one should raise the way an undeclared producer does (registry pattern: `authoritative_for` cites docs/audits/ via AUDIT_CITATION_PREFIX; reuse it). Inputs for the row: (1) what 0019 shows — NO exception is warranted today (kind 15 → WI-bamar producer fix; is_exported 41 → INV-huboz merge-pass fix; name 65 → vocabulary question, owner's), so the built-in table ships EMPTY and the config key is the extension point; (2) the two declared levels to move into the same table: CORROBORATED_CONFIDENCE 0.95 (merge_producers) and SUPERSEDED_STUB_RANK_FACTOR 0.5 (finalize); (3) incumbency is still INFERRED from ALTERNATIVE_BACKENDS={\"scip\"} in registry.incumbent_first — this row should make the per-language producer order a declared default (built-in = the inferred order, so 0019's numbers do not move) and expose the resolved incumbent so check_recorded_producer_input reads it instead of the constant; (4) unknown keys raise (user_config._KNOWN_SETTINGS), config tiers are ADR-0045 preferences (user + project both allowed: the default executes nothing); (5) merge_producers.merge_producer_records and finalize.demote_superseded_stubs take the resolved values as parameters, cli threads them, defaults unchanged — so every existing fixture number stays pinned. A regenerated 0019 after this row must be byte-identical above `## Reading` (that is the acceptance test that the default did not move)."  # 7c3d
