- op: discuss  # aab1
  at: '2026-09-19T09:47:08Z'  # aab1
  by: agent  # aab1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # aab1
  clock: 7  # aab1
  nonce: aab1  # aab1
  message: "Done in PR #1080 (dev e60e6abe43). The arbitration default is now a preference: `hypergumbo_core/arbitration.py` — `ArbitrationPolicy(prefer, prefer_by_attribute, corroborated_confidence, superseded_stub_rank_factor)`, `BUILTIN_POLICY` (incumbent first via the registry's `incumbent_first`, 0.95, 0.5, no per-attribute exception), `policy_from_config` / `resolve_arbitration_policy` over the ADR-0045 tiers, and `BUILTIN_ATTRIBUTE_EXCEPTIONS` + `validate_builtin_exceptions` (the §10 citation gate: a built-in exception must cite a docs/audits/ document of kind backend_agreement; the shipped table is EMPTY because 0019 warranted none — kind 15 → WI-bamar, is_exported 41 → INV-huboz). The two declared levels moved into the policy module and are re-exported from merge_producers / finalize under their old names.\n\nConfig (both tiers, `user_config._KNOWN_SETTINGS` + `[merge.prefer_by_attribute.<attr>]` prefix rule; unknown keys still raise):\n  [merge] prefer = [\"scip\", \"tree-sitter\"]; corroborated_confidence = 0.95; superseded_stub_rank_factor = 0.5\n  [merge.prefer_by_attribute] kind = [\"scip\"]   # replaces `prefer` for that attribute\nOrders name BACKENDS (declared by some registered analyzer — validated), attributes must be TRACKED_ATTRIBUTES, levels in [0,1] (bool refused), project tier replaces user tier key by key. Wired: run_survey resolves the policy BEFORE indexing (bad key → exit 2 naming file and key, no analysis run) and threads it to merge_producer_records(policy=) — precedence, per-attribute precedence, §13 level — and FinalizeContext.arbitration_policy → demote_superseded_stubs(policy=) — producer order, §14 factor. The lint reads registry.incumbents_of (ALTERNATIVE_BACKENDS stays the fact about which arm is the alternative; precedence is the policy's).\n\nBehavioural evidence (acceptance from the item): test_merge_pass_in_pipeline.py::test_a_user_preference_changes_the_contested_scalar_and_nothing_else — a config.toml with `[merge.prefer_by_attribute] kind = [\"scip\"]` changes Alias's kind variable → type_alias (attribution [pyscip], alternatives [variable/python]) and every other (name, kind, origin, span) tuple of the artifact is identical to the built-in run; test_an_unknown_merge_key_exits_two_naming_the_file_and_key — `[merge] prefers = [...]` in .hypergumbo.toml → exit 2, stderr names .hypergumbo.toml and merge.prefers. On the recorded aardvark-dns fixture (test_recorded_fixtures.py::test_a_kind_preference_for_scip_moves_exactly_the_kind_row) a kind preference for scip moves exactly the kind row's carried value (shape constant ← variable x15) and no other count; the committed 0019 table is unchanged under the built-in. Unit: 16 policy/config tests (test_arbitration.py), 3 merge-pass policy tests, 1 finalize factor test. Eight mutations (order ignores prefer; per-attribute ignored in the policy and in the merge pass; config prefer dropped; level range; bool accepted; project tier ignored; finalize factor hardcoded) each kill 1–5 tests.\n\nNot done, stated: no CLI flag or environment variable spells a precedence (ADR-0045 ruling 4's upper rungs) — no measurement has asked for a one-off override, and adding a knob with no reader is rule 7; incumbency per language is not declared on the registration (the item's open question) — precedence is now declared by policy and the alternative-arm fact stays in ALTERNATIVE_BACKENDS, which the next LSP-backed backend extends by one entry."  # aab1
